                <pb facs="0338" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 294/24a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-20T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 20,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>91. For your information. Identic note to the Allied Powers on subject of payment
                    of costs of our Army of Occupation is being cabled to you today.<anchor n="55"
                        xml:id="d181-f1"/> In view of publicity already given here and abroad,
                    Department will release note to Press on Wednesday afternoon<anchor n="56"
                        xml:id="d181-f2"/> for publication here in morning papers Thursday. To
                    ensure that the note will not be published in Europe before it is published
                    here, have note delivered to the Foreign Office on Wednesday afternoon. Similar
                    instructions are being sent Embassies at London, Brussels, Rome and Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
